@startuml
title System Architecture - FocusDesktop

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #333333
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F1F1F1
  BorderColor #333333
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #F1F1F1
  BorderColor #333333
}

node "Learner Workstation" {
  node "Desktop Client (Tauri)" {
    component "React + TypeScript UI\nTimer · History · Analytics · Settings" as UI
    component "Tauri Shell\nwindow · tray · OS integration" as Tauri
  }

  node "Local Backend Process (Spring Boot)" {
    component "Inbound Adapters\nREST Controllers + WebSocket" as Inbound
    component "Application Layer\nUse Cases · DTOs · Ports" as App
    component "Domain Layer\nAggregates · VOs · Services · Events" as Domain
    component "Outbound Adapters\nJPA · OS hooks · Clock · Event Publisher" as Outbound
  }

  database "Local Database\nH2 (MVP) / SQLite (later)" as DB
  component "Operating System\nActive window · process control\nscreen capture (Phase 3)" as OS
}

UI --> Inbound : HTTP/JSON\n127.0.0.1 + token
UI <--> Inbound : WebSocket\ntimer + domain events
Tauri ..> UI : hosts

Inbound --> App : commands / queries
App --> Domain : business rules
App --> Outbound : ports
Outbound --> DB : JDBC / JPA
Outbound --> OS : native APIs

note right of DB
  No cloud dependency.
  All productivity data stays
  on the learner's workstation.
end note

note bottom of Domain
  Dependency rule: the domain layer has
  no dependency on Spring or infrastructure.
end note

note bottom of Inbound
  The local API binds to 127.0.0.1 only
  and requires a per-installation token.
end note

@enduml
